'''Shinbetsu''' (神別) refers to one of the classifications of [[ancient]] [[Japan]]'s [[Uji (clan)|clans]].

The ''{{ill|Shinsen Shōjiroku|ja|新撰姓氏録}}'' compiled during the [[Heian period]] describes Shinbetsu alongside ''{{ill|Kōbetsu|ja|皇別}}'' and ''{{ill|Shoban|ja|諸蕃}}'', identifying the descendants of ''{{ill|Amatsukami|ja|天津神}}'' and ''{{ill|Kunitsukami|ja|国津神}}'' as "Shinbetsu" ("天神地祇之冑、謂之神別"). Furthermore, Shinbetsu is categorized into ''{{ill|Tenson|ja|天孫}}'', ''{{ill|Amatsukami|ja|天津神}}'', and ''{{ill|Kunitsukami|ja|地祇}}'', with Tenson accounting for 109, Amatsukami for 265, and Kunitsukami for 30 entries. These classifications are thought to have ancient origins, as inferred from the concentration of ''{{ill|Omi|ja|臣}}'' titles among ''{{ill|Kōbetsu|ja|皇別}}'' clans and ''{{ill|Muraji|ja|連}}'' titles among Shinbetsu clans under the pre-[[Ritsuryō system]].

