{{afc comment|1=I am exhausted by the sorting, is anyone else interested in sorting it?[[User:Immanuelle|Immanuelle]] ([[User talk:Immanuelle|talk]]) 21:22, 30 March 2025 (UTC)}}
{{afc comment|1=There does not seem to be a comprehensive list on japanese wikipedia, or anywhere so compiling the list from different sources[[User:Immanuelle|Immanuelle]] ([[User talk:Immanuelle|talk]]) 07:27, 27 March 2025 (UTC)}}

'''Shinbetsu''' (神別) refers to one of the classifications of [[ancient]] [[Japan]]'s [[Uji (clan)|clans]].

The ''{{ill|Shinsen Shōjiroku|ja|新撰姓氏録|1=Shinsen Shōjiroku|qq=draft|qq=draft}}'' compiled during the [[Heian period]] describes Shinbetsu alongside ''{{ill|Kōbetsu|ja|皇別|qq=draft|qq=draft}}'' and ''{{ill|Shoban|ja|諸蕃|qq=draft|qq=draft}}'', identifying the descendants of ''{{ill|Amatsukami|ja|天津神|qq=draft|qq=draft}}'' and ''{{ill|Kunitsukami|ja|国津神|qq=draft|qq=draft}}'' as "Shinbetsu" ("天神地祇之冑、謂之神別"). Furthermore, Shinbetsu is categorized into ''{{ill|Tenson|ja|天孫|qq=draft|qq=draft}}'', ''{{ill|Amatsukami|ja|天津神|qq=draft|qq=draft}}'', and ''{{ill|Kunitsukami|ja|地祇|qq=draft|qq=draft}}'', with Tenson accounting for 109, Amatsukami for 265, and Kunitsukami for 30 entries. These classifications are thought to have ancient origins, as inferred from the concentration of ''{{ill|Omi|ja|臣|qq=draft|qq=draft}}'' titles among ''{{ill|Kōbetsu|ja|皇別|qq=draft|qq=draft}}'' clans and ''{{ill|Muraji|ja|連|qq=draft|qq=draft}}'' titles among Shinbetsu clans under the pre-[[Ritsuryō system]].

The ancestral deity of a shinbetsu clan is their [[Oyagami]] and will also be an [[Ujigami]] although some clans may have other Ujigami such as the '''{{ill|Fujiwara clan|ja|藤原氏|qq=draft|qq=draft}}''' whose three Oyagami are [[Ame-no-Koyane]], [[Himegami]] and {{ill|Ame-no-Oshikumone|ja|天押雲根命|qq=draft|qq=draft}}, however the two are worshipped alongside two non-ancestral Ujigami: [[Takemikazuchi]]-o, and [[Futsunushi]]. The five are merged together into the composite deity {{ill|Kasuga-no-Kami|ja|春日神|1=Kasuga-no-Kami|2=ja|3=春日神|4=fr|5=Kasuga no Kami|6=zh|7=春日權現|8=wuu|9=春日權現|fr|Kasuga_no_Kami|qq=draft|qq=draft}} worshipped at [[Kasuga-taisha]] and many other Kasuga shrines nationwide.

